1.1.text:
Article 13

(1) The provision of services for the Empowerment and Protection of Women as referred to in Article 11 paragraph (4) letter j, shall include:

a. identification of victims of criminal violence;
b. legal assistance;
c. medical rehabilitation;
d. psychosocial rehabilitation;
e. social reintegration;
f. repatriation assistance; and
g. other forms.
(2) Services for the Empowerment and Protection of Women as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be provided to women who are:
a. victims of violence;
b. victims of human trafficking;
c. in conflict-prone and disaster areas;
d. workers;
e. elderly;
f. persons with disabilities;
g. victims of sexual exploitation;
h. heads of households;
i. pregnant and/or breastfeeding; and
j. other vulnerable victims.

Article 11

(1) The Regent establishes policy programs and activities for the empowerment and protection of women to eliminate all forms of discrimination and violence against Women.

(2) The implementation of policies, programs and activities as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out by Regional Apparatus responsible for the empowerment and Protection of Women.

(3) The Regional Apparatus as referred to in paragraph (2) may cooperate with the community, universities, community organizations, other regency/city governments, and/or international institutions in empowerment and Protection of Women activities.

(4) Forms of cooperation as referred to in paragraph (3) shall be carried out through:

a. policy analysis;
b. implementation coordination;
c. advocacy;
d. socialization;
e. public communication;
f. information delivery;
g. education;
h. training;
i. service facilities;
j. service provision;
k. model development; and
l. other activities.
(5) Integration of policies, programs and activities for the empowerment and Protection of Women as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be set forth in the following documents:
a. Regional long-term development plan;
b. Regional medium-term development plan; c. Regional Apparatus strategic plan;
d. Regional Government work plan; and
e. Regional Apparatus work plan and budget.
(6) Provisions regarding the establishment of policies, programs and activities for the empowerment and Protection of Women as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be stipulated by Regent Decree.

Article 2

Every woman has the right to:

a. live and improve her standard of living;
b. security;
c. a good and healthy living environment;
d. establish a family and continue offspring;
e. work and receive fair wages for her work;
f. obtain proper education;
g. obtain care, education, training and/or special assistance;
h. personal freedom; and
i. health.

